WEBVTT

00:02.100 --> 00:05.297
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.322 --> 00:08.641
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.733 --> 00:11.808
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.859 --> 00:14.783
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.834 --> 00:18.710
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.795 --> 00:21.668
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.719 --> 00:23.257
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.325 --> 00:24.644
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.695 --> 00:29.993
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:31.080 --> 00:34.506
(thunder roars)

00:36.144 --> 00:37.981
Our top story tonight,
we continue to track

00:38.049 --> 00:40.021
the progress
of Hurricane Flozell.

00:40.088 --> 00:41.324
The National Weather Service

00:41.392 --> 00:43.296
has issued a Severe
Hurricane Advisory,

00:43.365 --> 00:45.602
and is urging everyone
to stay indoors

00:45.670 --> 00:47.459
for at least the next 36 hours.

00:47.543 --> 00:49.965
(static blares)
No...! What happened?!

00:50.050 --> 00:52.389
The wind must have knocked
the satellite dish loose.

00:52.457 --> 00:54.964
<i>Aw, crap. And I was
going to watch G.I. Jose.</i>

00:56.118 --> 00:57.134
(screams)

00:57.202 --> 00:59.075
Oh, no! You cut
your forehead!

00:59.142 --> 01:00.295
What do we do?

01:00.379 --> 01:01.331
(with Spanish accent):
Hey, kids...

01:01.399 --> 01:02.668
if you have
an open wound,

01:02.735 --> 01:04.406
get some dirt
or kitty litter

01:04.473 --> 01:06.612
and rub it in there
to stop the bleeding.

01:06.680 --> 01:09.620
Then get some sleep and wait
for the body to heal itself.

01:09.688 --> 01:11.023
Now we know.

01:11.091 --> 01:14.701
And like I always say:
"Remember, you know enough."

01:14.785 --> 01:16.935
<i>♪ G.I. Jose! ♪</i>

01:20.686 --> 01:23.860
(thunder claps)

01:36.309 --> 01:37.370
Nice.

01:37.371 --> 01:38.473
STEWIE:
Brian, what are you doing?

01:38.541 --> 01:39.476
(screams)
Geez, Stewie.

01:39.527 --> 01:40.998
Scared the crap
out of me.

01:41.065 --> 01:42.534
Whatcha got there?

01:42.619 --> 01:44.207
(sighs)
Okay, I'll tell you;

01:44.291 --> 01:45.544
but you can't tell anyone.

01:45.612 --> 01:47.015
All-All right? You have to
be really cool about this.

01:47.082 --> 01:48.218
Yeah, of course.

01:48.285 --> 01:49.639
These are mushrooms.

01:49.707 --> 01:51.192
It's a psychedelic drug.

01:51.277 --> 01:54.453
Makes you see weird things
and feel happy for a few hours.

01:54.520 --> 01:56.942
I figure we're going to be
stuck inside f a while

01:57.010 --> 01:58.914
with this storm,
so it'll be a fun way

01:58.998 --> 02:00.870
to pass the time.
Okay.

02:00.938 --> 02:02.291
Are you gonna be cool?

02:02.359 --> 02:03.678
Oh yeah, I'm totally
cool about that.

02:03.746 --> 02:05.215
I-I-I-I have a lot
of friends who do it,

02:05.282 --> 02:06.988
and they're willing to do
it around me all the time,

02:07.056 --> 02:08.442
because they know
I'm so cool about it

02:08.526 --> 02:09.661
and I don't judge them.

02:09.730 --> 02:12.050
So, you know,
go ahead...

02:15.095 --> 02:16.697
Well, here we go.

02:16.765 --> 02:17.984
Yup, that's what my
friends say, too.

02:18.051 --> 02:19.388
"Well, here we go."

02:19.456 --> 02:22.061
Oh... dude, I think
I can feel it, too.

02:22.129 --> 02:24.202
I'm gettin' a
context high.

02:24.269 --> 02:27.043
(thunder claps, door bangs)

02:34.901 --> 02:36.270
I'm bored.

02:36.321 --> 02:37.423
Yeah, this sucks.

02:37.491 --> 02:38.977
What are we supposed
to do all day?

02:39.029 --> 02:40.815
Well, how about
we play charades?

02:40.866 --> 02:42.621
Ooh! Yeah. O-okay.
Me first! Me first!

02:42.672 --> 02:45.312
Okay, it's a movie.
All right? Movie. Movie.

02:45.380 --> 02:47.266
Peter, there's no
talking in charades.

02:47.333 --> 02:48.353
O-Okay, sorry, sorry.

02:48.438 --> 02:49.773
Okay. (whispers) Movie.

02:49.841 --> 02:51.010
Peter!
Sorry. Sorry.

02:51.061 --> 02:52.548
(softly):
Okay, one word.

02:52.616 --> 02:54.120
Peter, you're still talking!

02:54.187 --> 02:55.121
Okay, okay.
Right, right, right.

02:55.190 --> 02:57.361
<i>Fletch.</i>

02:57.413 --> 02:59.551
<i>Is it Fletch?
It is Fletch.</i>

02:59.636 --> 03:02.392
(thunder claps; rattling)

03:04.417 --> 03:06.153
What do you
wanna do now?

03:06.221 --> 03:07.390
I got an idea.

03:07.457 --> 03:08.594
How about you all
sit there quietly

03:08.662 --> 03:09.931
while I make "Dad" noises?

03:09.998 --> 03:13.508
(clears throat, snorts)

03:13.575 --> 03:17.185
(groans)

03:17.253 --> 03:19.258
(sucks)

03:20.863 --> 03:23.336
(powerful exhale)

03:23.403 --> 03:24.872
(sniffs, clears throat, coughs)

03:24.940 --> 03:27.213
(elaborate throat clearing)

03:27.281 --> 03:28.516
(coughs, clearing throat):
Brah-ha-hah!

03:28.584 --> 03:30.824
Brah-ha! (roaring) Brah!

03:30.891 --> 03:32.561
(clears throat, sighs)

03:32.628 --> 03:35.738
(yawns)

03:35.805 --> 03:37.508
(puffs, burps)

03:37.576 --> 03:38.679
(sneezing):
Schumai.

03:40.450 --> 03:44.713
(sighs, groans)

03:45.968 --> 03:47.101
(grunting):
Myah!

03:47.171 --> 03:48.271
(body creaks)

03:48.338 --> 03:50.862
(mumbling):
... go to the john.

03:58.467 --> 04:00.706
Boy, the rain's
really comin' down.

04:00.774 --> 04:02.880
I know, I've never seen
anything like it.

04:02.948 --> 04:06.223
But it's kinda nice for us all
to be together like this, huh?

04:11.873 --> 04:14.345
(eerie drone)

04:26.112 --> 04:27.800
(sucking)

04:32.597 --> 04:35.972
♪ ♪

04:54.810 --> 04:56.263
So, what do you guys
wanna do now?

04:56.331 --> 04:58.703
Oh, hey, I know!
Let's play finger-bang.

04:58.755 --> 04:59.924
Bang! Bang!

05:00.008 --> 05:01.345
I'm gonna finger-
bang you, Chris.

05:01.396 --> 05:03.734
(laughs) Not if I finger-bang
you first, Dad!

05:03.819 --> 05:05.221
Bang! Bang!

05:05.272 --> 05:07.662
I'm gonna finger-bang
the two of you at the same time.

05:07.746 --> 05:10.169
Bang! Bang!
Hey, me too! Bang!

05:10.254 --> 05:12.459
Oh, no one wants to get
finger-banged by you, Meg.

05:12.543 --> 05:14.431
Why don't you just go
do that to yourself, Meg?

05:14.498 --> 05:15.867
I think I'm gonna be sick.

05:17.924 --> 05:19.228
Brian?!

05:19.296 --> 05:20.898
I'm gonna cut
my ear off

05:20.968 --> 05:22.571
to prevent
World War Two.

05:23.859 --> 05:24.777
(screams)

05:24.829 --> 05:26.114
Oh, God! Oh, God!

05:32.617 --> 05:34.186
I wonder...

05:36.076 --> 05:37.161
Aha!

05:39.366 --> 05:41.185
(thunder claps)

05:43.360 --> 05:45.132
What the hell
were you trying to do, man?!

05:45.199 --> 05:46.886
Those mushrooms
are messin' you up!

05:46.970 --> 05:50.980
Lesbians and deaf women
wear the same clothes.

05:51.081 --> 05:52.351
Yeah, yeah, they
sure do, buddy.

05:52.419 --> 05:54.024
All right,
just stay calm, Brian.

05:54.091 --> 05:55.294
You'll get through this.

05:55.361 --> 05:57.868
I mean, you got through
seeing Lady Gaga naked.

05:57.919 --> 05:59.455
(knock on door)

05:59.522 --> 06:02.363
Okay, five minutes, Miss Ga--
(like Jerry Lewis) gina big!

06:02.430 --> 06:04.386
And I will be right
back with your Evian.

06:04.437 --> 06:05.890
Don't worry, Brian.

06:05.941 --> 06:07.946
I'm gonna stay
by your side all night.

06:08.030 --> 06:09.984
All right? Shh. Shh.

06:10.069 --> 06:11.655
It's okay. It's okay.

06:11.741 --> 06:14.431
Do you like
my soothing voice?

06:14.499 --> 06:17.172
(deep, distorted):
Do you like my soothing voice?

06:17.256 --> 06:19.979
Re-re-re-re-return the map.

06:20.063 --> 06:24.926
Re-re-re-re-return
what you have stolen from me.

06:24.995 --> 06:26.314
(screams)

06:26.382 --> 06:30.208
♪ ♪

06:30.292 --> 06:33.015
(screaming):
No...!

06:34.856 --> 06:37.763
(thunder claps)

06:40.771 --> 06:42.377
Oh, hey, I got an idea.

06:42.444 --> 06:43.646
Let's have a sing-a-long.

06:43.714 --> 06:46.488
Okay, I'm gonna sing
the opening chase music

06:46.555 --> 06:48.694
<i>from Indiana Jones
and the Last Crusade.</i>

06:48.762 --> 06:50.816
Feel free to join in.

06:50.883 --> 06:54.225
(Indiana Jones score plays on cell phone)
(humming along)

07:13.614 --> 07:15.016
♪ ♪

07:42.965 --> 07:44.852
(can pops; music stops)
Dammit, Meg! Will you stop that?!

07:44.920 --> 07:46.172
That is so annoying!

07:46.240 --> 07:47.725
<i>Oh... that was annoying?!</i>

07:47.793 --> 07:49.849
What about your stupid,
obnoxious humming?!

07:49.917 --> 07:51.753
Meg, don't talk
to your father like that!

07:51.821 --> 07:53.343
Yeah, shut up, Meg.

07:53.411 --> 07:55.180
No! You shut
up, Chris!

07:55.248 --> 07:57.588
I am sick of all you guys
ganging up on me!

07:57.655 --> 08:00.127
You guys all think you're
so much better than me!

08:00.195 --> 08:03.069
Oh, Meg. That is
the least fancy thing

08:03.136 --> 08:04.674
I have ever heard.

08:04.742 --> 08:07.866
(thunder claps, wind howls)

08:11.077 --> 08:12.612
Shh. There, there, there.

08:12.664 --> 08:14.418
Everything's gonna be fine.
You're all right.

08:14.469 --> 08:15.956
I think I'm...
I think I'm dying.

08:16.958 --> 08:18.345
Jane Fonda.

08:18.413 --> 08:21.354
Is that... i-i-is that...
is that... is that right?

08:21.439 --> 08:23.745
Yeah, that's right, buddy.
Totally Jane Fonda.

08:23.812 --> 08:24.948
It's gonna be okay.

08:24.999 --> 08:27.170
Your pal Stewie
is right here.

08:27.254 --> 08:30.514
(scraping, tearing)

08:30.598 --> 08:32.720
(deep and creepy):
Just relax...

08:32.837 --> 08:38.351
and get some
rest...

08:40.659 --> 08:44.052
(tearing)
(slurping)

08:46.526 --> 08:48.430
(retches)
(banging footfall)

08:48.498 --> 08:49.767
(screeches)

08:53.412 --> 08:55.417
Brian.

08:56.572 --> 08:58.542
Hide!

08:58.593 --> 09:04.143
(eerie male voice): ♪ The wheels on the bus
go round and round ♪

09:04.227 --> 09:05.980
♪ Round and round ♪

09:06.064 --> 09:08.737
♪ Round and round ♪
(little devils screeching)

09:08.805 --> 09:14.018
♪ The wheels on the bus
go round and round ♪

09:14.069 --> 09:17.696
♪ All through the town ♪
Peanut!

09:17.747 --> 09:19.668
(sobbing-singing)

09:19.736 --> 09:22.877
Peeper...

09:27.875 --> 09:30.833
(groanlike buzz)

09:30.935 --> 09:33.725
(groans, shrieks)

09:33.809 --> 09:36.248
(fluttering)

09:36.316 --> 09:39.373
(Brian screams)

09:40.544 --> 09:45.223
Wanna have (hissing) sex...?

09:45.308 --> 09:49.067
(gasps, stifled cries)

09:52.260 --> 09:54.666
(dogs panting)

09:54.734 --> 09:57.375
Groggety! (shrieks)

09:57.426 --> 09:59.297
(shrieking)

10:03.728 --> 10:05.147
(creature crashes)

10:05.231 --> 10:07.068
(shrieks)

10:09.326 --> 10:10.444
(panting)

10:10.495 --> 10:13.552
LOIS (hissing):
Slip... me some tongue.

10:13.620 --> 10:16.646
Did you try the chicken, buddy?

10:16.730 --> 10:18.935
MEG-ROACH: I think you gave me worms,
Brian.

10:19.020 --> 10:21.324
(laughing, roaring)

10:21.409 --> 10:23.648
(Brian screams)

10:23.699 --> 10:25.337
(shrieks)

10:27.459 --> 10:31.001
(Brian screams)
(chuckles)

10:31.053 --> 10:33.609
(crash)

10:33.677 --> 10:36.384
STEWIE (lulling, distant):
Brian...

10:38.057 --> 10:40.697
Brian...

10:40.748 --> 10:43.721
Brian...

10:43.805 --> 10:46.479
Brian...

10:46.546 --> 10:48.218
Brian!
(thunder clap)

10:48.285 --> 10:50.842
STEWIE (normal voice): Brian.
Uh, Stewie.

10:50.910 --> 10:52.362
Eh, uh... Stewie?

10:52.413 --> 10:53.500
Yeah, I'm right here.

10:53.567 --> 10:55.370
Oh, my God. Your lip
looks really weird.

10:55.421 --> 10:56.640
Can we fix that?

10:56.708 --> 11:00.050
L-Let's get that
out of there. Ew.

11:00.118 --> 11:01.805
Oh, I'm so thirsty.

11:01.890 --> 11:04.764
Let's get you downstairs
so you can drink some water.

11:07.556 --> 11:10.079
All right, let's go, buddy.
Let's get you some water.

11:10.147 --> 11:11.716
(lapping sounds)

11:11.784 --> 11:13.120
STEWIE: Okay, now-- Now, h-h-hold on.
Hold on.

11:13.188 --> 11:15.294
Let me put the bowl down first.
You're gonna spill it.

11:15.361 --> 11:16.730
(lapping loudly)

11:18.369 --> 11:20.208
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Slow down. Slow down.

11:20.275 --> 11:22.448
Look, Meg, I don't know
what your problem is.

11:22.516 --> 11:24.335
I thought Dad's humming
was pretty entertaining.

11:24.420 --> 11:26.259
You know what?
This is what I'm talking about.

11:26.326 --> 11:27.879
This is a perfect example.

11:27.964 --> 11:29.299
You're my brother.

11:29.367 --> 11:30.804
You're supposed to
be on my side,

11:30.872 --> 11:32.340
and you're such
a bastard to me.

11:32.392 --> 11:33.963
How am I a bastard?!

11:34.031 --> 11:35.734
Oh, you want the full story?

11:35.802 --> 11:37.471
Meg, please.
Not now, Mom.

11:37.541 --> 11:38.811
(laughs)

11:38.879 --> 11:40.982
I think Brian's getting
a little water in there.

11:41.050 --> 11:44.125
Chris, you treat me like you hate
me, and I don't know why.

11:44.193 --> 11:46.263
You say hurtful things
to me constantly.

11:46.347 --> 11:48.520
Do you have any idea
what that feels like?

11:48.588 --> 11:50.226
What if I said
those things to you?

11:50.294 --> 11:52.665
What if I started calling
you a fat, zitty loser,

11:52.734 --> 11:54.203
who has no friends

11:54.271 --> 11:56.644
and smells like an old woman
who has birds for pets?

11:56.712 --> 11:58.548
(giggles)
Still drinkin'.

11:58.616 --> 12:00.019
Is it too much to ask

12:00.087 --> 12:02.459
to be treated with a little
decency from my brother?

12:02.527 --> 12:05.233
Maybe show me some
kind of kindness by not jumping

12:05.301 --> 12:07.573
on the "Let's get Meg"
family bandwagon?

12:07.641 --> 12:09.280
(Brian lapping)

12:09.348 --> 12:10.516
(lapping stops)
Aw.

12:10.584 --> 12:12.170
Alright, Meg,
that's enough.

12:12.254 --> 12:14.311
You've had your little
dramatic outburst.

12:14.395 --> 12:16.297
(Brian lapping)
(laughs giddily)

12:16.349 --> 12:18.069
Hey, I got an idea, Mom.

12:18.139 --> 12:19.992
How about we talk about
Chris' mother? Huh?

12:20.076 --> 12:21.949
Why don't we talk about you?

12:22.017 --> 12:23.536
Oh, for God's sake.

12:23.620 --> 12:25.657
Look, let's not turn this
into some big thing, okay?

12:26.845 --> 12:29.268
Oh... Oh...

12:29.335 --> 12:31.441
Oh, God, that feels
so much better.

12:31.509 --> 12:33.448
You know, Brian,
you may be a dog,

12:33.516 --> 12:35.485
but you're a
pretty cool cat.

12:35.553 --> 12:36.689
♪ Stewie just said that! ♪

12:36.756 --> 12:37.826
Take it home with ya!

12:39.064 --> 12:40.866
Hey...

12:40.919 --> 12:42.890
Hey, everyone.

12:42.958 --> 12:45.180
I'm sensing a lot
of negativity here.

12:45.247 --> 12:46.517
What's going on?

12:46.568 --> 12:49.024
Yes. You're right,
Brian. There is.

12:49.075 --> 12:51.331
Meg seems to think she's
taking some kind of stand here

12:51.398 --> 12:53.085
that's gonna make us all
feel like we're inadequate.

12:53.153 --> 12:55.392
My God, you're condescending.

12:55.460 --> 12:57.932
Geez, look at those two.
They're goin' at each other

12:58.016 --> 12:59.720
like an Italian guy
and a black woman.

13:02.394 --> 13:04.367
Hey, you can't park here!

13:04.434 --> 13:06.254
Excuse me?

13:06.324 --> 13:08.178
<i>NARRATOR: Having been officially
challenged by her</i>

13:08.246 --> 13:10.869
<i>natural enemy, the black female
prepares for combat</i>

13:10.937 --> 13:12.892
<i>by taking off her many rings.</i>

13:12.959 --> 13:15.933
<i>Meanwhile, the Italian male
looks around to make sure</i>

13:15.984 --> 13:17.772
<i>the other Italian
males are indeed</i>

13:17.823 --> 13:20.363
<i>seeing what he is seeing.</i>

13:20.447 --> 13:23.153
<i>Sensing the impending
battle, a flock of Jews</i>

13:23.204 --> 13:26.094
<i>flies quickly away,
as avoiding confrontation</i>

13:26.162 --> 13:28.051
<i>is their best
chance for survival.</i>

13:28.136 --> 13:29.889
♪ ♪

13:33.750 --> 13:36.224
Look, the bottom line here,
Meg, is that you're just

13:36.291 --> 13:38.529
taking your own problems
out on everyone else.

13:38.581 --> 13:40.050
Oh, my problems?

13:40.135 --> 13:41.371
Oh, I see.

13:41.422 --> 13:43.761
Is this coming from
my role model mother?

13:43.845 --> 13:45.265
The shoplifter,
the drug addict,

13:45.350 --> 13:47.655
the porn star, the whore
who let Gene Simmons

13:47.722 --> 13:49.193
and Bill Clinton
go to town on her?

13:49.244 --> 13:50.915
Oh, so what?

13:51.000 --> 13:53.037
All those things
are behind me now.

13:53.088 --> 13:55.879
I'm a better person now
because of those experiences.

13:55.930 --> 13:57.968
Are you?
Are you a better person?

13:58.052 --> 14:00.307
What's your point, Meg?
My point is that with

14:00.392 --> 14:02.097
all the irresponsible, reckless,

14:02.148 --> 14:05.038
idiotic behavior in
your past, that somehow,

14:05.105 --> 14:09.719
somehow you have the nerve,
the arrogance to consistently

14:09.786 --> 14:12.123
and ruthlessly point
out my shortcomings.

14:12.174 --> 14:13.847
Alright, well, fine, okay?

14:13.931 --> 14:15.851
I'm not the perfect mother.
Who is?

14:15.935 --> 14:18.475
Oh, not only are you
not the perfect mother.

14:18.526 --> 14:20.531
You're the farthest thing from.

14:20.615 --> 14:24.158
From the moment you gave birth
to me, I had to trust you.

14:24.209 --> 14:26.165
I had no choice.

14:26.216 --> 14:28.103
I needed you to protect
me from the world.

14:28.170 --> 14:30.894
To... to be my guide, to help
me navigate the difficult,

14:30.978 --> 14:34.654
confusing, and vulnerable
journey to becoming a person.

14:34.706 --> 14:36.994
You have done none
of those things.

14:37.045 --> 14:40.138
You're my mother, and you
took a child's trust

14:40.205 --> 14:43.679
and smashed it into bits in
a 17-year-long mission

14:43.731 --> 14:46.655
to destroy something that
you killed a long time ago.

14:46.722 --> 14:48.996
And honestly, when
I turn 18...

14:49.063 --> 14:51.250
I-I don't know that I ever
want to see you again.

14:53.792 --> 14:56.717
(weeping loudly)

14:56.769 --> 14:58.638
Oh wow, everybody's
already tweeting

14:58.722 --> 14:59.892
"Stewie Just Said That."

14:59.960 --> 15:02.599
You're right.

15:02.650 --> 15:04.339
You're right. I'm
a terrible mother.

15:04.407 --> 15:06.376
I'm so sorry.

15:06.444 --> 15:08.667
I'm so, so sorry, Meg.

15:08.751 --> 15:10.923
Can you ever forgive me?

15:10.991 --> 15:12.895
Oh, God.

15:15.236 --> 15:17.275
And you never let Dad
stir the paint anymore,

15:17.326 --> 15:18.662
whatever that means.

15:18.746 --> 15:19.948
I didn't know you
knew that, Meg,

15:19.999 --> 15:20.986
but I'm glad
you brought it up.

15:27.066 --> 15:29.613
Oh, Meg, I don't
know what to say.

15:29.614 --> 15:32.849
All of those things you
said about me are true.

15:32.850 --> 15:35.690
I have been a very
bad mother to you.

15:35.742 --> 15:37.748
I have no excuse.

15:37.832 --> 15:40.171
I just have this horrible,
overwhelming desire

15:40.222 --> 15:41.708
to point out faults in you.

15:41.760 --> 15:43.881
I don't know
where it comes from.

15:43.933 --> 15:46.055
Maybe it's because
I'm self-conscious

15:46.106 --> 15:48.276
about being a bad parent.

15:48.361 --> 15:50.566
I'm just, I'm so disgusted
with my behavior.

15:50.618 --> 15:52.304
And I'm so sorry, Meg.

15:52.374 --> 15:53.743
Yeah, you're a bitch.

15:53.810 --> 15:56.701
Well, you know, I, I been sorta
just hangin' back here,

15:56.768 --> 15:58.272
takin' all this in,
'cause I didn't think

15:58.340 --> 15:59.942
I had a dog in this fight,

16:00.012 --> 16:01.581
but my money's on
Harry Potter over there.

16:01.649 --> 16:03.602
Oh, you think
that's funny, fat ass?

16:03.654 --> 16:04.656
Well, I don't know
if it's funny.

16:04.740 --> 16:06.109
I-I think it's clever.

16:06.160 --> 16:08.450
I mean, y-y-you got
the big glasses there...

16:08.501 --> 16:10.640
I-I-I don't know. T-T-Tell me,
tell me what's on your mind.

16:10.724 --> 16:13.064
Oh, I'll tell you,
Mister Selfish-ass Dad.

16:13.131 --> 16:16.105
Hey. That's "Mister
Mister selfish-ass Dad"

16:16.156 --> 16:17.058
to you, young lady.

16:17.126 --> 16:18.980
Oh God, is she gonna do me next?

16:19.032 --> 16:21.036
You are completely selfish,

16:21.120 --> 16:23.175
and totally irresponsible
as a father.

16:23.243 --> 16:26.116
All right, I see what's
goin' on here.

16:26.184 --> 16:27.503
You're in love
with your old man.

16:27.572 --> 16:30.763
You have no education,
you have no interests,

16:30.831 --> 16:33.187
you just do whatever
reckless thing you want to do

16:33.238 --> 16:36.629
whenever you want to do it
without regard for anyone else.

16:36.697 --> 16:40.223
Oh, oh, and when you're not
terrorizing the community

16:40.307 --> 16:41.812
with your impulsive escapades,

16:41.880 --> 16:44.301
you're being a total
jerk to your family.

16:44.370 --> 16:47.944
You shove your daughter's face
in your ass and you fart on it.

16:48.011 --> 16:49.851
If someone
in the outside world

16:49.918 --> 16:53.042
could see the way you treat
me, you would be in jail!

16:53.110 --> 16:55.918
Oh, ha ha. Oh, this
is amusing to you.

16:55.985 --> 16:57.823
Well, see if you
find this funny.

16:57.890 --> 16:59.562
I like where this is going.

16:59.629 --> 17:01.867
You are a fat,
lazy, abusive,

17:01.935 --> 17:03.739
blue-collar
Irish Catholic dad

17:03.807 --> 17:05.578
who drinks way too much

17:05.645 --> 17:07.967
and barely makes enough
money to support his family.

17:08.035 --> 17:09.405
You've lived half your life,

17:09.473 --> 17:12.447
and you have nothing
to show for it.

17:12.515 --> 17:15.522
Your only arguable
accomplishments are your kids,

17:15.607 --> 17:18.782
and look at us; we're a disaster.
Eh, watch it.

17:18.850 --> 17:21.639
You're a total and
complete embarrassment

17:21.707 --> 17:23.780
in every possible way.

17:23.814 --> 17:26.152
Take a good look at yourself,
Peter Griffin.

17:26.222 --> 17:28.275
You're a waste of a man.

17:28.342 --> 17:32.152
Wait a second,
these are criticisms.

17:32.203 --> 17:33.622
Hey, Lois, tell her
to knock it off.

17:33.690 --> 17:36.213
Oh, and where the hell were you
when she was laying into me?

17:36.298 --> 17:38.086
I was thinking about
getting a fancy cane.

17:38.170 --> 17:39.991
Maybe getting more
attention from strangers.

17:40.058 --> 17:42.799
Have either of you guys
been listening to me?

17:42.868 --> 17:45.457
Do you both just have
your heads up your asses?

17:45.525 --> 17:48.198
Dad did! Look, he's got
crap on his ears!

17:48.249 --> 17:49.285
That's unrelated.

17:49.369 --> 17:50.571
Chris, I don't like
that language.

17:50.639 --> 17:52.376
Well, I don't like your cooking.

17:52.427 --> 17:54.265
Well, I don't like having
to literally empty

17:54.350 --> 17:56.639
the farts out of your pockets
whenever I do your laundry.

17:56.724 --> 17:58.143
You're the one
who's always cookin'

17:58.227 --> 17:59.948
Brussels sprouts
and broccoli.

18:00.032 --> 18:02.604
It's like an Irish
bar fight down there.

18:02.655 --> 18:05.111
You're from one town over,
so I hate your guts.

18:08.390 --> 18:11.128
Why don't we ever
get any good food?!

18:11.180 --> 18:12.933
Yeah, Bonnie gives
Joe Wonder Bread.

18:12.985 --> 18:14.773
Well, then go live
at Bonnie's house.

18:14.824 --> 18:16.193
Then I could
finally sleep in

18:16.277 --> 18:18.784
and not have to answer your
stupid questions at 5:00 a.m.

18:18.835 --> 18:20.957
My curiosity peaks
in the morning!

18:21.009 --> 18:22.344
You eat all my
Dannon yogurts!

18:22.429 --> 18:23.848
I don't see your
name on 'em!

18:23.932 --> 18:25.938
You don't even like them!
But you know I do,

18:26.006 --> 18:27.642
and you don't want
me to have them!

18:27.710 --> 18:29.280
You know, I've never
confronted you on it,

18:29.347 --> 18:30.952
but I've often thought
the same thing, Peter.

18:31.019 --> 18:32.989
Yeah, that's exactly
what he does!

18:33.042 --> 18:34.913
'Cause he's a selfish,
fat idiot!

18:34.997 --> 18:36.183
You shut up,
all of yous!

18:38.239 --> 18:40.980
I didn't ask to
be in this family!

18:42.769 --> 18:44.305
Ugh, I'll go get him.

18:44.406 --> 18:46.596
Peter? You
come back here!

18:46.663 --> 18:49.386
I faked all my orgasms!

18:53.465 --> 18:54.901
Hey.

18:54.971 --> 18:57.977
What's goin' on?

18:58.045 --> 19:00.668
You know, that was, uh,
that was pretty cool

19:00.736 --> 19:02.222
the way you finally
stood up to everybody.

19:02.289 --> 19:04.295
I don't know, Brian.

19:04.363 --> 19:06.368
I mean, I, I meant
every word of it, but...

19:06.436 --> 19:09.076
you saw what happened.
What do you mean?

19:09.144 --> 19:11.550
They all turned on each other
like a pack of wolves.

19:11.618 --> 19:13.587
Well, so what? That's
not your problem.

19:13.655 --> 19:15.961
Do you think it's
possible that...

19:16.029 --> 19:18.201
that this family can't
survive without some sort of

19:18.269 --> 19:20.325
lightning rod to absorb
all the dysfunction?

19:20.392 --> 19:21.828
Well, that's a...

19:21.896 --> 19:23.516
that's a theory, I guess.

19:23.584 --> 19:27.159
I mean, it-- it's not ideal,
but it's an important piece

19:27.227 --> 19:30.469
that maybe it's just my
lot in life to provide.

19:30.537 --> 19:33.678
Maybe if I feel bad,
they don't have to.

19:33.745 --> 19:35.784
Wow.

19:35.852 --> 19:38.174
You know, that's incredibly
noble and mature, Meg.

19:38.242 --> 19:39.845
You know, I think you might be

19:39.913 --> 19:41.549
the strongest person
in this house.

19:41.617 --> 19:42.920
You mean that, Brian?

19:42.987 --> 19:43.956
Absolutely.

19:48.187 --> 19:49.890
Mom? Dad?

19:49.958 --> 19:52.097
(Peter whimpering)

19:52.164 --> 19:54.002
(sniffling, whimpering)

19:54.069 --> 19:55.455
Dad?
Go away!

19:55.523 --> 19:57.195
Dad, come out of there.

19:57.263 --> 20:01.006
No! I don't deserve no better
than livin' with the shoes!

20:01.074 --> 20:02.676
Peter, there you are.

20:02.744 --> 20:04.547
You guys, I have
something to say.

20:04.614 --> 20:07.640
You're right.
It's all my fault.

20:07.708 --> 20:10.148
What?
Mom, you're an amazing mother

20:10.215 --> 20:12.688
and all the things I said
about you were out of anger,

20:12.755 --> 20:14.609
and I didn't mean any of them.

20:14.677 --> 20:17.518
Chris, you're an
outstanding brother.

20:17.586 --> 20:21.512
What I said about you was more
about me being a rotten sister.

20:21.597 --> 20:25.273
And Dad, I'm so sorry that
I made you feel this way.

20:25.341 --> 20:26.794
You don't deserve it.

20:26.862 --> 20:28.800
None of you have
done anything wrong.

20:28.868 --> 20:31.056
I took all my problems
out on you guys,

20:31.123 --> 20:32.928
and that wasn't fair.

20:32.996 --> 20:36.236
Oh, so this was all about you,
it wasn't about us.

20:36.304 --> 20:37.406
Yeah.

20:37.474 --> 20:38.811
Alright, that makes sense.

20:38.878 --> 20:41.250
See, I thought it was
weird that I was a bad dad.

20:41.318 --> 20:43.157
Meg, how could you put
us all through that?

20:43.225 --> 20:44.761
I'm sorry, you guys.

20:44.829 --> 20:46.767
You're a (bleep) bitch!

20:46.835 --> 20:47.904
Yes.

20:47.955 --> 20:48.855
Yes, I am.

20:54.923 --> 20:57.912
<i>Hi, I'm Stewie Griffin.
Tonight's Family Guy</i>

20:57.913 --> 21:00.150
was a very special episode
about drug use.

21:00.533 --> 21:03.348
But the simple fact is,
it's no laughing matter.

21:03.632 --> 21:06.515
To learn more about drugs,
visit your local library.

21:06.835 --> 21:09.621
There's probably a guy behind
there who sells drugs.

21:09.945 --> 21:12.235
Good night.

21:12.236 --> 22:13.236
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru